m. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an abra around Route 24 / Route 25. It grows into my alakazam — that\'s my answer for Erika AND Koga down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "What? I\'m waiting for my friends to find me here."; "POK. BALL, and you want 1. That will be .200. Okay?"; "POK. BALL? Certainly. How many would you like?". YOUR PLAN — right now: get mankey and spearow to 15 before Mt. Moon. Next: Make your way to Cerulean City. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L23), mankey (L9), spearow (L9). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "1 badge(s) earned (Boulder). Next gym: Misty of Cerulean City. Pokédex: 4 caught. She's one badge in — the adventure's really starting (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L23), mankey (L9), spearow (L9)', 'goal': {'short': 'get mankey and spearow to 15 before Mt. Moon', 'medium': 'Make your way to Cerulean City', 'long': 'Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge'}} options=['head_to_gym', 'battle', 'travel:3,2', 'travel:3,3', 'travel:3,1', 'travel:3,5', 'travel:3,26']

